# libledger89

A durable, append-only sequence of opaque records stored in immutable rotated
segments, with crash recovery and deterministic iteration, in strict ISO C89.

```text
            application
        +-----------------+
        | storage adapter |
        | timers/policy   |
        +--------+--------+
                 | append / sync / truncate
        +--------v--------+
        |   libledger89   |
        | durable local   |
        | record sequence |
        +--------+--------+
                 |
           segment files
```

libledger89 owns exactly one thing: a local, durable, append-only sequence of
opaque records. It knows nothing about Raft terms, leaders, agents, SQL,
indexes, queries, capabilities, or application semantics. It never interprets
record payloads.

## Boundaries

| Concern | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| record encoding envelope | `libledger89` |
| monotonic local sequence | `libledger89` |
| append durability | `libledger89` |
| segment creation/sealing/rotation | `libledger89` |
| crash recovery | `libledger89` |
| checksums / corruption detection | `libledger89` |
| sequential/range iteration | `libledger89` |
| suffix truncation | `libledger89`, when explicitly requested |
| prefix discard (retention) | `libledger89`, when explicitly requested |
| replication | `libraft89` |
| deciding commit | caller / `libraft89` integration |
| semantic event format | application |
| secondary indexes, SQL, queries | external query engine |
| snapshots and projections | external component |

## Build and test

- `just build` — build `build/libledger89.a`.
- `just smoke` — one end-to-end open/append/sync/reopen/read path.
- `just unit` — pure unit programs (format, checksums, index math).
- `just api` — black-box public API behavior.
- `just adapters` — consumer-boundary fixtures (replication-style usage).
- `just crash` — crash points over the deterministic model filesystem and
  real-filesystem process kills.
- `just fault` — I/O errors, ENOSPC, allocation failure, torn writes.
- `just corrupt` — structural corruption classification.
- `just model` — randomized reference-model stress.
- `just stress` — many-segment, huge-payload, and recovery stress.
- `just bench` — reproducible throughput baseline (not part of `just test`).
- `just golden` — verify the committed on-disk byte fixtures; regenerate with
  `just golden-gen` and review the diff.
- `just test` — all fast suites.
- `just long` — multi-million-operation model runs plus a heavy many-segment
  sweep.
- `just sanitize` — fast suites under ASan + UBSan.
- `just valgrind` — fast suites under valgrind memcheck.
- `just check` — green profile, lint, and all fast suites.
- `just build32` — best-effort 32-bit library build. This host has no 32-bit
  multilib (`gnu/stubs-32.h`, `crt1.o` are absent), so the recipe reports
  `SKIPPED`; 32-bit portability is exercised on hosts that provide multilib.

## Conventions

- Public API namespaced `ledger89_*`, declared in `include/ledger89.h`.
- On-disk format is fixed little-endian with CRC-32C; no native structs.
- Test-driven: scenario -> acceptance -> failing test -> minimal code ->
  refactor.
- `main` stays green; no commits or pushes without permission.

See `spec/ledger89-spec.md` for the normative contract and `.agent/` for the
concept, design, scenarios, and acceptance criteria.
